@* Triggers the page's own merged printer-status read (see IPrinterStatusReader) rather than doing
   its own I/O - the read now runs automatically once a printer is Ready/paired, so this button is
   a manual re-trigger of that same read ("Recheck Configuration"), not the original one-shot
   on-demand check. Results/errors are still rendered by the sibling CheckConfigurationResults
   component (sharing the same CheckConfigurationState), so this button can live in a page's sticky
   header while a long results table scrolls separately below. *@

@* No spinner glyph here even while State.Loading - PrinterVersionAlert's single "Checking printer
   configuration..." spinner already covers the whole merged read (this button is just disabled for
   its duration); a second spinner on the button itself would be redundant. *@
<md-outlined-button type="button" data-testid="check-configuration-button" disabled="@(State.Loading || Disabled)" @onclick="() => OnRecheck.InvokeAsync()">
    Recheck Configuration
</md-outlined-button>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public CheckConfigurationState State { get; set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>Disables the button without hiding it - e.g. while a factory reset is in progress.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised on click - the host page owns the actual IPrinterStatusReader call.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public EventCallback OnRecheck { get; set; }
}
